# Data

The real dataset (`coal_prices.xlsx`: Richards Bay 4800/5500/5700/6000 kcal NAR
and India 5500 kcal NAR prices, USD/t, daily, 2020-04 to 2024-06) is
**proprietary and is not included in this repository**. `*.xlsx` is git-ignored
so it cannot be committed by accident.

## Using your own copy

Put the file here (e.g. `data/coal_prices.xlsx`) and run:

```bash
python -m coal_forecast.train --data data/coal_prices.xlsx
```

Expected layout: first column = date (header may be blank), one column per
price series. A stray `Date`/`Price` row under the header is tolerated.
Series names are listed in `src/coal_forecast/config.py`; if none match,
every numeric column is used.

## Trying the pipeline without the real data

`sample/synthetic_coal_prices.csv` is **randomly generated** (see
`scripts/make_synthetic_data.py`). It has the same layout and column names but
no market meaning, so forecasts from it are for demonstration only.
